      "text": "Here's a summary of what I was able to confirm about the publication details of *Babel*:\n\n---\n\n## *Babel, or the Necessity of Violence: An Arcane History of the Oxford Translators' Revolution* — Publication Details\n\n**Full Title:**\n*Babel, or the Necessity of Violence: An Arcane History of the Oxford Translators' Revolution*\nThe subtitle is often dropped in casual references, but the complete title is important for your review.\n\n**Author:** R.F. Kuang (Rebecca F. Kuang)\n\n**Publisher:** **Harper Voyager** (an imprint of HarperCollins), published **August 23, 2022**\n\n**ISBN:** 978-0-06-313087-8\n\n**Page Count:** The exact page count varies slightly by edition/format (e.g., hardcover vs. paperback), and I wasn't able to pin down a single confirmed figure across sources — **545 pages** is the most commonly cited figure for the US hardcover, but this is worth double-checking against your physical copy or the publisher's catalogue, as different printings can differ by a page or two.\n\n**Alternate Titles / Editions:**\nMy research did not surface any evidence that the book was published under a *different title* in any market. Both the US and UK editions (Harper Voyager published it in both markets) use the same full title. There are no known alternate titles for other international markets, though translated editions naturally carry translated titles.\n\n---\n\n**A note of caution on the page count:** My sources returned strong metadata but did not produce a single locked-down page figure. For your review, I'd recommend verifying the page count directly from the publisher's page at HarperCollins.com or your copy of the book, as the most reliable source.",
